00:07:48.187 --> 00:07:50.541
Okay, what's your question after that?

00:07:50.541 --> 00:07:52.715
(hosts laugh)

00:07:52.715 --> 00:07:53.932
- Of course, where?

00:07:53.932 --> 00:07:55.152
- Where?
- Where?

00:07:55.152 --> 00:07:56.871
- I give you a time, you ask where.

00:07:56.871 --> 00:07:58.993
Okay, I say, "Chuck,
I'll meet you tomorrow

00:07:58.993 --> 00:08:01.247
"at the corner of 33rd and Third."

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:02.117
- [Chuck] When?

00:08:02.117 --> 00:08:02.950
- When.

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:07.242
We know intuitively that
our path through life

00:08:07.242 --> 00:08:09.967
involves the juxtaposition
of space and time.

00:08:09.967 --> 00:08:11.778
We know that, intuitively.

00:08:11.778 --> 00:08:14.109
We just don't think of it in those terms,

00:08:14.109 --> 00:08:16.778
because they're measured
by such different tools.

00:08:16.778 --> 00:08:18.861
A watch and a map, right?

00:08:20.097 --> 00:08:22.955
But in fact, they're
conjoined, and Einstein

00:08:22.955 --> 00:08:27.955
formalized that statement in
his theories of relativity.

00:08:28.262 --> 00:08:30.229
- Amazing.
- Yeah.

00:08:30.229 --> 00:08:31.752
